    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "One number is 9 less than twice another, and their sum is 42. Find the two numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$17$ and $25$.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the other number. Then the first number is $2x-9$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+(2x-9)&=42\\\\3x-9&=42\\\\3x&=51\\\\x&=17\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe first number is $2(17)-9=25$.\n\nTherefore, the two numbers are $17$ and $25$.",
